{title: Steadfast Love in the Morning}
{subtitle: Psalms 143:8}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I remember the days of old
Meditating on what [Cm]you have done
Pondering the work [Ab]of your hands
Stretching out to you [Eb]in the sun
My soul thirsts for you so [Bb]deep
Like a parched land with no sleep [Eb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Answer me quickly, Lord, [Cm]I pray
My spirit is spent a[Ab]way
Do not hide your face from [Eb]me
Or I will fall into the [Bb]pit
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Let [Eb]me hear of your steadfast love
In the morning, let it [Cm]move
For I trust in you alone
Show me the way I should [Ab]walk
[Bb]To you I lift up my [Eb]soul
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Deliver me from my enemies
To you I flee for cov[Cm]er
Teach me to do your [Ab]will
For you are my God, my [Eb]shelter
Let your good Spir[Bb]it lead
Me on level ground, in[Eb]deed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Let me hear of your steadfast love
In the morning, let it [Cm]move
For I trust in you alone
Show me the way I should [Ab]walk
[Bb]To you I lift up my [Eb]soul
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm]For your name's sake, Lord, pre[Ab]serve
My life, in your righteous[Eb]ness
Bring me out of trouble [Bb]now
Your grace is my only [Eb]peace
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] | [Ab] | [Bb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Steadfast love in the morning
I trust in you
{end_of_verse}
